      "writtenOn": "2017-01-13T16:39:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It should be fine.  SHA256 is collision resistant regardless of message size.  Assuming that fails, A hash digest mixes in the size of the hashed data (in SHA256_final()), so the attacker would need to find a collision which took that into consideration.\n\nIf we get worried about that, the ec_response_vboot_hash struct already contains the hashed offset/size, so AP-RW could verify that the correct portion of the image was hashed.  But I suspect if SHA256 collisiion attacks become practical we\u0027ve got much bigger problems.",
